{%- doc -%}
  Canonical float-frame key for any stored Frame option value. This is the
  single alias table for the storefront: current catalog values
  ("Oak Float Frame"), legacy aliases ("Oak frame", "wood") and bare colour
  names ("oak", "white") all resolve here, case- and whitespace-insensitively.

  Outputs oak | black | walnut | white | gold | silver, or nothing for
  canvas-only delivery (Rolled Canvas, Stretched Canvas, No frame) and for
  unknown values, so callers can fall back to a no-frame state.

  The JS twin is `window.theme.frameKey` in assets/utils.js; the two lists are
  kept identical by scripts/frame-aliases.test.js.

  @param frame {string} stored Frame option value
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign value = frame | default: '' | strip | downcase
  case value
    when 'oak float frame', 'oak frame', 'oak', 'wood'
      echo 'oak'
    when 'black float frame', 'black frame', 'black'
      echo 'black'
    when 'walnut float frame', 'walnut frame', 'walnut'
      echo 'walnut'
    when 'white float frame', 'white frame', 'white'
      echo 'white'
    when 'gold float frame', 'gold frame', 'gold'
      echo 'gold'
    when 'silver float frame', 'silver frame', 'silver'
      echo 'silver'
  endcase
-%}
